ok - an absent pyenv rehash lock is a silent, successful no-op
ok - an orphaned lock is moved aside with its contents intact, not deleted
ok - running the cleaner twice clears once and then says nothing
ok - a genuinely running rehash makes the cleaner refuse and leave the lock alone
ok - a live rehash executable path containing spaces is recognized and refused
ok - an ambiguous rehash identity stays unknown instead of using lock age
ok - a process that only mentions pyenv-rehash on its command line is not treated as the holder
ok - an unverified shell command mentioning pyenv-rehash stays unknown
ok - a long-orphaned lock is cleared even while blocked shells are still waiting on it
ok - a young lock is cleared when its only rehash started after the lock already existed
ok - a rehash that predates its lock keeps holding it however long it has been running
ok - a provable holder is refused at any lock age, including past the stale threshold
ok - an unreadable process table still clears a stale lock but never a young one
ok - the cleaner refuses arguments so it cannot be aimed at another path
ok - a symlink at the lock path is refused rather than moved
# all fm-pyenv-shim-lock tests passed
